as_code+='~t/**~r~n'
as_code+='~t * Helper function to fit a radial linear scale with point labels~r~n'
as_code+='~t */~r~n'
as_code+='~tfunction fitWithPointLabels(scale) {~r~n'
as_code+='~t~t/*~r~n'
as_code+='~t~t * Right, this is really confusing and there is a lot of maths going on here~r~n'
as_code+='~t~t * The gist of the problem is here: https://gist.github.com/nnnick/696cc9c55f4b0beb8fe9~r~n'
as_code+='~t~t *~r~n'
as_code+='~t~t * Reaction: https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/34601363/toomuchscience.gif~r~n'
as_code+='~t~t *~r~n'
as_code+='~t~t * Solution:~r~n'
as_code+='~t~t *~r~n'
as_code+='~t~t * We assume the radius of the polygon is half the size of the canvas at first~r~n'
as_code+='~t~t * at each index we check if the text overlaps.~r~n'
as_code+='~t~t *~r~n'
as_code+='~t~t * Where it does, we store that angle and that index.~r~n'
as_code+='~t~t *~r~n'
as_code+='~t~t * After finding the largest index and angle we calculate how much we need to remove~r~n'
as_code+='~t~t * from the shape radius to move the point inwards by that x.~r~n'
as_code+='~t~t *~r~n'
as_code+='~t~t * We average the left and right distances to get the maximum shape radius that can fit in the box~r~n'
as_code+='~t~t * along with labels.~r~n'
as_code+='~t~t *~r~n'
as_code+='~t~t * Once we have that, we can find the centre point for the chart, by taking the x text protrusion~r~n'
as_code+='~t~t * on each side, removing that from the size, halving it and adding the left x protrusion width.~r~n'
as_code+='~t~t *~r~n'
as_code+='~t~t * This will mean we have a shape fitted to the canvas, as large as it can be with the labels~r~n'
as_code+='~t~t * and position it in the most space efficient manner~r~n'
as_code+='~t~t *~r~n'
as_code+='~t~t * https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/34601363/yeahscience.gif~r~n'
as_code+='~t~t */~r~n'
as_code+='~r~n'
as_code+='~t~tvar plFont = getPointLabelFontOptions(scale);~r~n'
as_code+='~r~n'
as_code+='~t~t// Get maximum radius of the polygon. Either half the height (minus the text width) or half the width.~r~n'
as_code+='~t~t// Use this to calculate the offset + change. - Make sure L/R protrusion is at least 0 to stop issues with centre points~r~n'
as_code+='~t~tvar largestPossibleRadius = Math.min(scale.height / 2, scale.width / 2);~r~n'
as_code+='~t~tvar furthestLimits = {~r~n'
as_code+='~t~t~tr: scale.width,~r~n'
as_code+='~t~t~tl: 0,~r~n'
